ch Fire is such a special  show that was six years of my life I did  it with Chris Cantwell my dear friend uh  and the truth is you know many things  have to come together for a show to  happen we got our heart broken a couple  times after Hall and it wasn't until  paper girls came around that you know  the right thing shaped up again that we  could really put ourselves into and so I  do think this is in some ways the  spiritual error to some of the things we  are playing with in that series uh  certainly it starts in the 80s as well  but but it's awesome to be able to  approach new territory I I think with  some of the lessons learned from that  show so so it's been awesome to kind of  stretch our wings and can you give us an  example of a specific lesson learned  that you actually applied to paper girls  but then also even with all your  experience what's something about what  it took to show her on paper girl is  that caught you by surprise 100 I think  the most important thing I learned on  Halt and Catch Fire is you have to let  this story speak to you uh there's a  story you set out to write and then  there's the story that wants to happen  and on this show you know we showed up  with these wonderful characters that we  took from the comics but then we cast  these wonderful actresses and they want  to be a little different they want to  bring things to the characters that  maybe aren't envisioned and you need to  listen to that and go with it and just  as we did that on Halt and let that show  go to places we never envisioned when we  set out I think each of these girls has  changed the fundamental four characters  of the comics in a in a way I just found  so beautiful and I can take no credit  for all right so kind of jumping off of  that Cliff for you even though you  worked on the source material here what  is something about even your own work  that was even stronger than you ever  realized when it was brought to screen  it's like even though you made it when  you saw it in this particular format  through this Medium you're like whoa  like that is way more powerful than I  ever could have imagined it would be  yeah I don't know if there are like  specific instances of it it's kind of  like the whole project has the same  heart and feel that we put into the  comic book and and that's so  um incredibly I'm so grateful for that  um you know the writers the whole team  and the actresses they really I think uh  you know accepted the story really  assimilated it and and want to kind of  put out this new version of it that's  expanded and you know in many ways just  you know just uh just an incredible New  Vision for it I hate asking this  question because it makes me feel greedy  because season one hasn't even come out  but again I love your show I'm gonna  want more when you start a process like  this do you need to map out a series  overview for yourselves before you even  jump into season one of the show yeah I  mean I think it's that Hold On Loosely  but don't let go I think we know some  places we'd like to get but we are open  to better ideas winning out we  absolutely have a direction planned for  a second season and I just hope that  God's smile on us and we get to do it I  say this a lot I'm a big believer in  manifesting so that's my excuse to ask  that question to follow up on that a  little is there anything about your  experience working on season one that  let you walk away with a new tool new  lesson that now you plan to apply to  season two going forward just that I I  think this show is all about tone uh and  it's all about the girls together in the  certain register they're able to live in  when they're interacting with each other  when they're bringing themselves to the  characters and I think the more we can  feed into that into their relationships  with one another because I think this  ultimately is kind of a love letter to  their friendship that's that's home for  us you know the time travel all the  other exciting Adventures it matters and  its Story by the end of the day we  really care about these girls in their  journey and when we're writing that when  we're performing that and we're seeing  that I think we're really doing paper  girls right you were very very  successful that is one of my favorite  qualities of the series you made just so  it's on camera I'm going to say this one  last thing to you Brian it's not a  question it's just a statement why the  last man deserved to run on and on you  did exceptional work with that you did  exceptional work here seriously  everybody out there make sure you watch  paper girls thank you guys for your time  thank you
 

